Here's my suggestion for 3.1:

When you polymorph several things (say over 5), there is a chance
that you will create a demon (either by polymorphing one of the 
objects into a demon, or perhaps by polymorphing the bugs on the 
floor).

The probability increases depending on the number of items.  The
type of demon might depend on your level or the dungeon level.

Why add this?

Polypiling is a great trick (Yes, I am a chronic polypiler :).
I don't think it's a nethack bug or abuse, I think it's a feature. 
However, with any good feature I believe there should be some
risk when overused.  This is true of enchanting weapons or armor.
Why not polymorphing?

An alternate hazard might be to have a chance of making the wand
disappear if you try to polymorph too much.  Or perhaps a risk of 
all the objects you polymorph evaporating.  Or, if you used a spell 
of polymorph, the spell could be forgotten, or the spell could 
polymoph itself into something else.  

